.Dd $Mdocdate: {{mdocdate}} $
.Dt {{daemon_name | upcase}} 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm {{daemon_name}}
.Nd example daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm {{daemon_name}}
.Op Fl dnv
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a template daemon.
It detaches from the terminal, logs to
.Xr syslogd 8 ,
listens on a control socket for
.Xr {{ctl_name}} 8
and runs a periodic task.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Do not daemonize.
If this option is specified,
.Nm
will run in the foreground and log to
.Em stderr .
.It Fl f Ar file
Specify an alternative configuration file.
.It Fl n
Configtest mode.
Only check the configuration file for validity.
.It Fl s Ar socket
Use
.Ar socket
instead of the path given in the configuration file to communicate with
.Xr {{ctl_name}} 8 .
.It Fl v
Produce more verbose output.
Once enables debug messages, twice enables trace messages.
.El
.Pp
When
.Cm user
is set in the configuration file,
.Nm
must be started as root: the control socket is created, handed to that
user, and privileges are dropped before the main loop starts.
.Pp
.Nm
refuses to start when another instance answers on the control socket.
A stale socket left by a crashed instance is removed.
.Pp
The following signals are handled:
.Bl -tag -width SIGTERM
.It Dv SIGHUP
Reload the configuration file.
On error the running configuration is kept.
Changes to
.Cm socket
and
.Cm user
take effect only after a restart.
.It Dv SIGTERM , Dv SIGINT
Terminate.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /var/run/{{daemon_name}}.sock -compact
.It Pa /etc/{{daemon_name}}.conf
Default configuration file.
.It Pa /var/run/{{daemon_name}}.sock
Default control socket.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check the configuration file:
.Pp
.Dl # {{daemon_name}} -n
.Pp
Run in the foreground with debug output on a private socket:
.Pp
.Dl $ {{daemon_name}} -dv -s /tmp/{{daemon_name}}.sock -f {{daemon_name}}.conf
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr {{daemon_name}}.conf 5 ,
.Xr {{ctl_name}} 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An {{author_name}} Aq Mt {{author_email}}
